From fc9a572c60f5ab6326a6e84f9db36cfd3438a1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:54:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hlg: HLG as Dolby Vision is automatic where the output cannot
 send HLG, takes the SEI that says HLG, and works in Low-Latency

Three things that the first version left out.

Automatic. videoscreen.hadeshlgasdv is now automatic (the default), on or off. Automatic sends an
HLG video as Dolby Vision only where this output cannot send HLG (its connector has no
HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA, as i915 has none for HDMI of display version 9 in Linux 7.3, or the display
declares no HLG) and the display takes native Dolby Vision: the one way for the video to keep its
HDR, where Kodi maps it to SDR. It is decided as Hdr10AsDolbyVision() decides it for HDR10 (and
<video><dvfromhdr10whenneeded>false</...> of advancedsettings.xml holds for both). Everywhere else
HLG plays as HLG. On sends it wherever the display takes Dolby Vision; Off never. The log says
which and why. HlgAsDolbyVisionFor() takes the mode and whether HLG can be sent.

The alternative transfer characteristics SEI. FFmpeg 9.0.2's HEVC decoder (hevc/hevcdec.c,
export_stream_params_from_sei()) sets the transfer of every picture to the preferred one of that
SEI (payload 147) when it names a transfer other than unspecified, so a stream with a VUI of
BT.2020 10-bit (14) and the SEI 18, as DVB broadcasts have them, is decoded as HLG, and so it is
HLG here: CDVHdr10Plus reads the SEI of each access unit (AccessUnit::alternativeTransfer) and
DVBRIDGE::HlgTransferOf() takes the decoder's rule. The stream's own parameters are looked at too.
Where the demuxer's probe has not decoded a picture they say 14 and only the SEI says HLG.

Low-Latency (player-led). HLG sent as Dolby Vision is drawn by the path that maps a picture to the
display, with the picture as HLG: libplacebo shows it as BT.2100 says an HLG picture is shown on a
display of the peak of the target (the system gamma follows that peak; no tone mapping, HLG signal
1.0 at the display's peak), not guided by the level 1 of the metadata, which is measured for a
display of 1000 cd/m2. The refusal of the first version is gone.

Strings: core 41152 to 41154 and Estuary 32633 to 32635 (the values), the help rewritten, with the
Spanish of es_es, es_ar and es_mx.

Checked on Mesa's software OpenGL ES: the picture in Low-Latency for a display of 800 cd/m2,
against an independent BT.2100 computation (gamma 1.2 + 0.42 log10(800/1000)), 6912 points a
picture within 0.36 codes of 10 bits (tolerance 2: libplacebo's gamma form is 1.2 * 1.111^log2),
and the same check fails by 25 codes against 1000 cd/m2; the picture at 1000 and the bytes of
every PQ picture as in the commits before. The SEI: seven synthetic streams (the units of a real
stream, VUI of 14, 16 or 18 with the SEI 18, 16, 2 or none) read by the real DVHdr10Plus.cpp
against what the FFmpeg 9.0.2 decoder gives their pictures: it says HLG exactly where the decoder
does. The policy, 397 checks against its plain statement over every combination (mode, display,
output, choice, advancedsettings) and three mutated policies that it rejects. 89 files compile.
Not seen on a display: the LG C5 game-mode input (Low-Latency only) is the hardware item for it.
